      "Run a slash command in your Discord server and Open Everywhere acts as an autonomous teammate — it does the work, replies in the channel, and remembers what it learned, scoped correctly per channel.",
      "",
      "This page is the Discord-specific setup runbook. For the concept of a *surface* and how surfaces plug in, see [Surfaces](../../extending/surfaces.md). For how memory is scoped per server and channel, see [Memory](../../capabilities/memory.md). For how Discord's feature set compares to the other surfaces — including what needs the Gateway relay and why — see the [surface support matrix](./support-matrix.md).",
      "",
      "**Discord has two ingestion paths, and this page sets up both.** The HTTPS **interactions** endpoint is interaction-based: on it, the only way to invoke the agent is an explicitly-registered slash command, and a plain `@mention` does nothing. Ambient `@mention`s, DMs, name-drops and channel follow-ups arrive over the separate **Gateway** path instead, which needs the always-on relay ([`deploy/discord-relay/`](../../../deploy/discord-relay/README.md)) — Discord never delivers those to an HTTP endpoint. The [surface support matrix](./support-matrix.md) marks every Gateway-dependent row with footnote ¹.",
      "",
      "## How the silo model maps",
      "",
      "Open Everywhere's memory is [opt-in domains and silos](../../capabilities/memory.md), not an",
